        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71131586?u=b6972c1f15e894240a92164b10f28809f53be4ef&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Remove outdated warning on accessibility roles in the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;summary&gt;</code> element.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The implicit role of the element was changed from <code class=\"notranslate\">button</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">no corresponding role</code> in the aria specifications at the end of 2022:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1433284006\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/html-aria/issues/434\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/html-aria/pull/434/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/html-aria/pull/434\">w3c/html-aria#434</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1433479038\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/html-aria/issues/435\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/html-aria/pull/435/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/html-aria/pull/435\">w3c/html-aria#435</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Seems like the <code class=\"notranslate\">implicit role</code> was corrected on mdn in 2023 (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1854113034\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28602\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/28602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/28602\">#28602</a>), but this specific warning was forgotten.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Although the specifications still contain <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/#el-summary\" rel=\"nofollow\">a warning</a> that browsers will still use a button role, I tested this and found it to not be the case at least in Chromium, Firefox and Safari. So perhaps the specs also need to be updated.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Relates to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1854113034\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28602\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/28602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/28602\">#28602</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40165",
            "title": "Remove Summary a11y warning",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-04T16:00:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-01T21:22:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "leekeh",
                "url": "https://github.com/leekeh"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 138 adds the CSS <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-5/#progress\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">progress()</code></a> function — see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112558941634560\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112558941634560</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds docs for the <code class=\"notranslate\">progress()</code> function.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note: The final demo code snippets are out of sync with the version available in the <code class=\"notranslate\">dom-examples</code> repo. You can find the latest updates added in this PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3193223045\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/issues/314\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/dom-examples/pull/314/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/pull/314\">mdn/dom-examples#314</a>. I'll keep it open until the reviews are done, in case there are further changes to make.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40159",
            "title": "Technical review: Add doc for CSS progress() function",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-03T10:05:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-01T16:52:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44144724?u=678ea4d3e126d07aa186e2e2d66337cb7e15ca44&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added a usage note to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/vibrate\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.vibrate()</code></a> page, explaining that vibration may not work when a device is in Silent Mode or Do Not Disturb (DND) mode.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Many developers encounter issues where <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.vibrate()</code> appears to do nothing, even though the API is supported and called correctly. After extensive debugging, I found that the root cause was that my phone was in Silent Mode, which disables vibration for web APIs. This behavior is undocumented and non-obvious, so this note will save other developers time and confusion.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40143",
            "title": "Add important note explaining why `navigator.vibrate()` may not work",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-30T19:10:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T19:09:53.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "babakfp",
                "url": "https://github.com/babakfp"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55658154?u=72eb5d6b966bd3197516e3205b1e2f4962df3cc6&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't see section #corb in <a href=\"https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#corb\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#corb</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the most related official document of corb I can found.<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.chromium.org/Home/chromium-security/corb-for-developers/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.chromium.org/Home/chromium-security/corb-for-developers/</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
